 Install htop                                                                                                 
                                                                                                              
 Why not `pacman -Sy htop`? It syncs the database and installs one package on a system                        
 that isn't fully upgraded: a partial upgrade. The package is built against libraries newer                   
 than yours, and things break later. cronen never does that.                                                  
      https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/System_maintenance#Partial_upgrades_are_unsupported                    
                                                                                                              
   A  Full upgrade, then install htop recommended                                                             
      Dry run: pacman -Sup --dbpath /tmp/checkup-db-1000 --logfile /dev/null --noconfirm --print-format       
      '%n %v %r %s' -- htop                                                                                   
      This runs: sudo pacman -Syu -- htop                                                                     
