      The temporary pacman.conf keeps your [options] and enables only core, extra, each with just the         
      archive Server.                                                                                         
      Left out: 2 Include lines.                                                                              
      The archive is slow. The next -Syu upgrades it normally. Root will read the config from                 
      /home/demo/.cache/cronen/archive/20261023T120000Z-test0001/2026-10-21, a directory cronen just created  
      (new for every install, 0700, written fresh); cronen compares it with what it wrote, and checks that no 
      db.lck exists, right before the hand-off.                                                               
                                                                                                              
